    "https://utica.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204400": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Nursing Labs and Lectures",
      "description": "Utica University\nJob Posting: Adjunct - Nursing Labs and Lectures Utica University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct - Nursing Labs and Lectures Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct - Nursing Labs and Lectures Category: Adjunct Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Health Professions & Education Locations: Utica, NY Posted: Sep 2, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $900.00 - $1,166.00 Position ID: 204400 Share About Utica University: Located in the heart of Central New York, Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 as Utica College. We offer many of the advantages of a large university, such as undergraduate and graduate degree options, excellent academic programs, and outstanding faculty, but with an intimacy and a high degree of personal attention more closely associated with smaller private institutions. We empower learners to achieve their career and life goals through personally enriching experiences and outstanding educational pathways. At Utica University, we are committed to creating a working and learning environment where all people feel supported. Following our institutional values, we work to support diverse perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences in an equitable, respectful, and inclusive environment, while promoting freedom of expression and encouraging civil discourse. Job Description: Position Summary: Utica University is currently accepting applications for adjunct instructors to teach nursing labs and lectures. The Nursing Department, in the School of Health Professions and Education, is seeking adjunct instructors to teach in-person Nursing courses in Utica, NY. Requirements: Education and Experience: Master's degree or BS in Nursing and enrolled in a Master's degree program NYS Registered Nurse License required Must have a current BLS certification Three (3) years of clinical and/or academic experience Certifications: Current certifications in CPR, AED, and First Aid Skills/Abilities: Teaching experience, preferred Must have strong communication skills Additional Information: Applicants must apply to the Adjunct Portal. To apply please use the following link: https://www.utica.edu/hr/adjunct.cfm and click on \"APPLY NOW\" Salary based per contact hour: Lab: $900 per contact hour Lecture: $1,166 per contact hour Visa sponsorship is not available for this position EEO Statement Utica University is committed to equal opportunity and creating a welcoming work environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to veteran status, disability, citizenship status, domestic violence victim status, or protected status under applicable local, state, or federal law. Commitment to Supporting and Hiring Veterans Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 to offer options for higher education study to veterans returning from the Second World War. More than seventy years since veterans returned from WWII, this tradition of serving veterans is still held in high regard here at Utica University, and we are proud to welcome veterans as students and as valued members of our faculty and professional staff. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply to the Adjunct Portal. To apply please use the following link: https://www.utica.edu/hr/adjunct.cfm and click on \"APPLY NOW\" Offers are contingent on the completion of a post-offer background check, and official transcripts are required upon hire. URL: www.utica.edu/hr/adjunct.cfm Hide Main Navigation Utica University 1600 Burrstone Road, Utica, NY 13502"
