his rewarding job, please visit https://www.utica.edu/forms/adjunct-application/index.cfm for more information. Requirements: Education and Experience: Master's Degree in Education Certified and Licensed NYS Teacher Must have previous teaching experience. Supervisory Responsibility: This position will supervise our Education students. Driving Responsibility: This position requires travel, must have valid driver's license. Additional Information: Salary based per placement: $510.00 -$1,020.00 Visa sponsorship is not available for this position EEO Statement Utica University is committed to equal opportunity and creating a welcoming work environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to veteran status, disability, citizenship status, domestic violence victim status, or protected status under applicable local, state, or federal law. Commitment to Supporting and Hiring Veterans Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 to offer options for higher education study to veterans returning from the Second World War. More than seventy years since veterans returned from WWII, this tradition of serving veterans is still held in high regard here at Utica University, and we are proud to welcome veterans as students and as valued members of our faculty and professional staff. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply to the Adjunct Portal. To apply please use the following link: https://www.utica.edu/hr/adjunct.cfm and click on \"APPLY NOW\" Offers are contingent on the completion of a post-offer background check, and official transcripts are required upon hire. URL: www.utica.edu/hr/adjunct.cfm Hide Main Navigation Utica University 1600 Burrstone Road, Utica, NY 13502"
