    "https://utica.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205695": {
      "title": "Adjuncts for Communications and Media",
      "description": "Utica University\nJob Posting: Adjuncts for Communications and Media Utica University \n\tJob Posting: Adjuncts for Communications and Media Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjuncts for Communications and Media Category: Adjunct Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Arts & Sciences Locations: Utica, NY Posted: Oct 12, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Temporary Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $2,313.36 - $2,619.36 Position ID: 205695 Share About Utica University: Located in the heart of Central New York, Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 as Utica College. We offer many of the advantages of a large university, such as undergraduate and graduate degree options, excellent academic programs, and outstanding faculty, but with an intimacy and a high degree of personal attention more closely associated with smaller private institutions. We empower learners to achieve their career and life goals through personally enriching experiences and outstanding educational pathways. At Utica University, we are committed to creating a working and learning environment where all people feel supported. Following our institutional values, we work to support diverse perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences in an equitable, respectful, and inclusive environment, while promoting freedom of expression and encouraging civil discourse. Job Description: Position Summary: Utica University and the School of Arts and Sciences is currently accepting applications for adjunct instructors to the following courses: CMM 101 - Interpersonal Communication This course is designed to enable a student to become a better communicator by developing a more sophisticated understanding of the communication process and the opportunities and challenges it presents. We will explore how the style and content of communication influences personal identity, relationships, and goal achievement. The ultimate objective is to enable the student to optimize his/her strategic communication competencies in order to be better prepared to identify and solve personal, relational, and organizational problems. CMM 103 - Introduction to Public Speaking The ability to speak in public is a valuable tool in any career. This course examines fundamental principles of public speaking, focusing on informative and persuasive messages. Students will learn to choose interesting topics, research and organize content, and present speeches using effective vocal and nonverbal delivery skills. Other important elements of this course include an understanding of how to successfully address different audiences, how to effectively use presentation aids, and the role that public speaking plays in our world today. CMM 181 - Introduction to Mass Communication The mass media play a significant role in your life. Books, newspapers, magazines, movies, music, radio, television, and the Internet are sources of information and entertainment that provide a shared cultural experience. The mass media have also historically shaped our economy and continue to be powerful channels for commerce. Introduction to Mass Communication inspires you to look at the mass media from a historical and critical perspective, and encourages you to become an informed consumer of media. Requirements: Education and Experience: Bachelors of Arts in related field and previous relevant experience, required Masters degree in related field, preferred. Skills/Abilities: Teaching experience, preferred Must have strong communication skills Additional Information: Salary based per course: 3 contact hours, starting at and based on experience $2,313.36 Visa sponsorship is not available for this position EEO Statement Utica University is committed to equal opportunity and creating a welcoming work environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to veteran status, disability, citizenship status, domestic violence victim status, or protected status under applicable local, state, or federal law. Commitment to Supporting and Hiring Veterans Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 to offer options for higher education study to veterans returning from the Second World War. More than seventy years since veterans returned from WWII, this tradition of serving veterans is still held in high regard here at Utica University, and we are proud to welcome veterans as students and as valued members of our faculty and professional staff. Application Instructions: Applicants must apply to the Adjunct Portal. To apply please use the following link: https://www.utica.edu/hr/adjunct.cfm and click on \"APPLY NOW\" Offers are contingent on the completion of a post-offer background check, and official transcripts are required upon hire. URL: www.utica.edu/hr/adjunct.cfm Hide Main Navigation Utica University 1600 Burrstone Road, Utica, NY 13502"
    },
    "https://utica.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=200740": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Utica University\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy Utica University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Health Professions & Education Locations: Utica, NY Posted: May 20, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Faculty - Tenure Track Ref. No.: Unionized Position Code: AAUP Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $75,000.00 - $80,000.00 Position ID: 200740 Share About Utica University: Located in the heart of Central New York, Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 as Utica College. We offer many of the advantages of a large university, such as undergraduate and graduate degree options, excellent academic programs, and outstanding faculty, but with an intimacy and a high degree of personal attention more closely associated with smaller private institutions. We empower learners to achieve their career and life goals through personally enriching experiences and outstanding educational pathways. At Utica University, we are committed to creating a working and learning environment where all people feel supported. Following our institutional values, we work to support diverse perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences in an equitable, respectful, and inclusive environment, while promoting freedom of expression and encouraging civil discourse. Job Description: Position Summary: The Department of Physical Therapy at Utica University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-eligible Assistant Professor faculty position in the on-campus, entry-level Doctor of Physical Therapy Program. This is a 10-month appointment with an opportunity to expand responsibility for a leadership role as Department Chair. The target start date is August 1, 2026 Responsibilities: The candidate will primarily teach ground courses in the neuromuscular system curriculum. Courses are currently taught during the traditional fall and spring semesters. Based on departmental needs, the successful candidate may also teach in other content areas, including geriatrics, pediatrics, other systems (e.g., integumentary, genitourinary, etc.), and/or research. Additional teaching opportunities are available based on the candidate's areas of interest. The candidate will conduct research and service appropriate for the program expectations and successful tenure review. As a DPT Program faculty member, the candidate will participate in advising undergraduate and graduate students, as well as providing professional mentoring Requirements: Education and Experience: Terminal academic doctoral degree such as a PhD, EdD, DSc, or equivalent. ABD candidates may be considered for this position This position requires a minimum of six years of full-time higher education experience, with a minimum of three years of full-time experience as a core faculty member in a CAPTE entry-level physical therapist education program. Required License/Certification and Qualifications: The candidate must have a current unrestricted license or eligibility for PT licensure in New York State. Skills/Abilities: Contemporary expertise in neuromuscular physical therapy or ABPTS Certification A commitment to innovation and student-centered learning Evidence of an ongoing or developing scholarly agenda Ability to engage in service activities in the department, at the University, and in the surrounding community Ability to function well within a collegial, collaborative work environment. Additional Information: About the Department Established in 1993, the Department of Physical Therapy is part of Utica University's School of Health Professions and Education, which also includes programs in occupational therapy, nursing, health sciences, social work, Child Life and Family Science, educator preparation, and the newly launched Physical Education, Exercise Science, and Wellness program. The School fosters interprofessional education, research, and service opportunities both locally and nationally. The department enrolls a cohort of 36 DPT students annually and is supported by a core of talented, collaborative faculty members, many of whom have over a decade of experience and service in leadership roles at the state and national levels of the APTA. Facilities include a renovated clinical lab, anatomy and neuroscience labs, the Utica University Sports Dome (one of the largest indoor multi-sport facilities in North America), and access to the Nexus Center. Students benefit from integrated clinical experiences, wellness programming for older adults, and partnerships with local healthcare systems, including the new Wynn Hospital, opened in 2023. More information is available at: https://www.utica.edu/academics/programs/physical-therapy-doctorate Visa sponsorship is not available for this position EEO Statement Utica University is committed to equal opportunity, and creating a welcoming work environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to veteran status, disability, citizenship status, domestic violence victim status, or protected status under applicable local, state, or federal law. Commitment to Supporting and Hiring Veterans Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 to offer options for higher education study to veterans returning from the Second World War. More than seventy years since veterans returned from WWII, this tradition of serving veterans is still held in high regard here at Utica University, and we are proud to welcome veterans as students and as valued members of our faculty and professional staff. Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must upload the following documents: Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Statement Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Utica University 1600 Burrstone Road, Utica, NY 13502"
    },
    "https://utica.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204177": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer - Certified",
      "description": "Utica University\nJob Posting: Assistant Athletic Trainer - Certified Utica University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Athletic Trainer - Certified Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Athletic Trainer - Certified Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Utica, NY Posted: Aug 27, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full Time Exempt Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $62,400.00 - $62,400.00 Position ID: 204177 Share About Utica University: Located in the heart of Central New York, Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 as Utica College. We offer many of the advantages of a large university, such as undergraduate and graduate degree options, excellent academic programs, and outstanding faculty, but with an intimacy and a high degree of personal attention more closely associated with smaller private institutions. We empower learners to achieve their career and life goals through personally enriching experiences and outstanding educational pathways. At Utica University, we are committed to creating a working and learning environment where all people feel supported. Following our institutional values, we work to support diverse perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences in an equitable, respectful, and inclusive environment, while promoting freedom of expression and encouraging civil discourse. Job Description: Position Summary: Provides all intercollegiate student-athletes with the best possible athletic exercise and medical care as needed. The incumbent will seek out guidance and direction from the Head Athletic Trainer with the following major responsibilities. Sport focus to be determined, Responsibilities: Understands and adheres to the Utica University Athletic Department philosophy. Provides all intercollegiate student-athletes with preventive care and assessment including exercise prescription and kinesthetic analysis. Also provides injury rehabilitation using cryotherapy, ultrasound, electric stimulation, whirlpools, and open/closed kinetic chain exercise protocols. Utilize medical referrals as required with guidance from the Team Physician. Assists Head Athletic Trainer by providing practice and home game coverage of all intercollegiate athletic events as assigned. Travel as assigned. Assists in preparing and executing pre-participation screenings. Assists in keeping general inventory and supply records. Keeps contemporaneous and up to date, confidential medical records including history, daily treatment records, injury reports and physician referrals while in compliance with all current regulations. Coordinates team injury summaries with the appropriate head coach and Head Athletic Trainer. Works harmoniously with coaches, athletic staff, students, team physician, and constituents while adhering to team philosophies. Exhibits a strong work ethic while setting a positive example in action and appearance for students. Coordinates insurance information with appropriate university official. Submits student-athlete accident insurance claims when necessary. Takes an active role in the development of the department's strategic and operational plans as required by department leadership. Works closely with department supervisor to develop and implement operational goals that support departmental success. Responsible for working with supervisor and other team members to achieve successful results on all established individual and departmental goals and key performance indicators. May perform other related duties as assigned. Requirements: Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree required. 2 years collegiate athletic training experience preferred. Certifications: NATABOC (National Athletic Trainers' Association) certified, required. Must possess Professional CPR/AED or equivalent Skills/Abilities: Must be willing and able to travel as required. Must have excellent written and verbal communication skills. Must have working knowledge of Microsoft Word and Excel. Supervisory Responsibility: Supervise work-study students. Driving Responsibility: Must maintain a clean driving record as defined by University insurance carrier guidelines. Motor vehicle record will be monitored regularly using NYS License Event Notification Service or License Monitor, Inc. for out of state licenses. Will be required to attend van training annually. Travel: Travel is required. Additional Information: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position EEO Statement Utica University is committed to equal opportunity and creating a welcoming work environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to veteran status, disability, citizenship status, domestic violence victim status, or protected status under applicable local, state, or federal law. Commitment to Supporting and Hiring Veterans Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 to offer options for higher education study to veterans returning from the Second World War. More than seventy years since veterans returned from WWII, this tradition of serving veterans is still held in high regard here at Utica University, and we are proud to welcome veterans as students and as valued members of our faculty and professional staff. Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must upload and include the following information: Submit a resume and cover letter at time of application. Three (3) references are required to be listed on the application. These should be professional references, two of which must be current or former supervisors. Finalist will be contacted prior to reference checking. Offers are contingent on the completion of a post-offer background check, and official transcripts are required upon hire. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Utica University 1600 Burrstone Road, Utica, NY 13502"
    },
    "https://utica.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204709": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Utica University\nJob Posting: Assistant Director of Admissions Utica University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of Admissions Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director of Admissions Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Enrollment Management Locations: Utica, NY Posted: Sep 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $62,400.00 - $62,400.00 Position ID: 204709 Share About Utica University: Located in the heart of Central New York, Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 as Utica College. We offer many of the advantages of a large university, such as undergraduate and graduate degree options, excellent academic programs, and outstanding faculty, but with an intimacy and a high degree of personal attention more closely associated with smaller private institutions. We empower learners to achieve their career and life goals through personally enriching experiences and outstanding educational pathways. At Utica University, we are committed to creating a working and learning environment where all people feel supported. Following our institutional values, we work to support diverse perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences in an equitable, respectful, and inclusive environment, while promoting freedom of expression and encouraging civil discourse. Job Description: Position Summary: The Assistant Director of Admission is responsible for developing and executing undergraduate recruitment and enrollment strategies within an assigned geographic territory or market portfolio. Through a territory-management approach, the Assistant Director builds and maintains productive relationships with prospective students and families, high schools, community colleges, school counseling professionals, community-based organizations, and other recruitment partners. The Assistant Director manages prospective students through the enrollment funnel from initial engagement through application, admission, deposit, and matriculation. The position uses enrollment, yield, market, and travel-performance data to prioritize outreach and recommend recruitment activity. Territory ownership establishes primary responsibility for relationship and market development but does not limit shared application review, travel, event coverage, or other team assignments based on institutional priorities. The Assistant Director may be assigned responsibility for priority markets, student populations, community partnerships, or academic programs consistent with institutional enrollment goals and nondiscrimination requirements. The position supports the University's undergraduate enrollment goals through timely, accurate, student-centered, and ethical recruitment and admission practices. This position has an assigned territory that includes the NY Downstate and Metro region including New York City, Bronx, Long Island, Staten Island, Connecticut and New Jersey. Preference is for a qualified candidate who is based in Utica with recruitment travel to the NY Downstate and Metro region, however, a highly qualified candidate located within the assigned territory would be considered and offered a remote work opportunity. Responsibilities: Develops and manages an assigned recruitment territory or market portfolio, with responsibility for relationship development, prospective-student engagement, application activity, admitted-student conversion, deposit yield, and enrolled-student outcomes. Establishes and maintains relationships with high schools, community colleges, school counseling professionals, community-based organizations, alumni, and other partners that support the University's recruitment goals. Uses enrollment data and established dashboards to evaluate territory performance, identify opportunities, prioritize schools and markets, and recommend travel and outreach activity. Develops a territory recruitment plan informed by enrolled-student production, yield, market potential, student interest, relationship-building opportunities, and anticipated return on travel. Conducts recruitment travel, including high school and community college visits, college fairs, regional and national recruitment programs, counselor programs, and other approved activities. Extended fall and spring travel, evening work, and weekend responsibilities are required. Conducts individual and group meetings with prospective students and families on and off campus and provides accurate information regarding admission, academic programs, financial aid, campus life, and the enrollment process. Maintains timely and purposeful contact with prospective and admitted students through telephone, email, text messaging, virtual engagement, appointments, events, and other approved communication channels. Guides prospective students and families through the enrollment process, identifies barriers or unresolved concerns, and coordinates appropriate referrals and warm handoffs to Financial Aid and other University offices. Reviews undergraduate applications as part of the University's shared application-review process and renders admission decisions within established institutional criteria, procedures, and delegated authority. Maintains timely, accurate, and complete prospective-student and recruitment records in Slate, Banner, and other approved institutional systems. Evaluates admitted students for merit scholarship eligibility in accordance with the University's approved scholarship criteria and awarding methodology. Monitors assigned funnel performance, including inquiries, applications, admits, deposits, yield, melt, and enrolled students, and adjusts individual outreach in consultation with admission leadership. Reviews the effectiveness of travel, school visits, fairs, and other recruitment activities and uses results to recommend continuation, modification, or discontinuation of activities. Participates in shared application review, recruitment travel, event coverage, and other enrollment activities outside the assigned territory when institutional priorities or workload require team deployment. Participates in open houses, accepted-student programs, daily visits, Saturday information sessions, counselor programs, and other on- and off-campus recruitment events. Collaborates with Enrollment Communications and Enrollment Technology to support coordinated, appropriately segmented, and timely outreach. Provides frontline observations and market information without independently developing or altering institutional communication plans or system processes. Collaborates with academic departments and other campus partners to provide prospective students with accurate program information and facilitate appropriate faculty engagement in recruitment. May serve as the admissions liaison for assigned academic programs, markets, community partnerships, or institutionally identified recruitment initiatives. Conducts all recruitment and admission activities in an ethical, equitable, respectful, and nondiscriminatory manner and provides consistent access to information and opportunities for prospective students. Contributes to the development and implementation of departmental strategic and operational plans. Works with the supervisor and other team members to achieve established individual, territory, and departmental goals and key performance indicators. Assists with daily office operations and performs other duties consistent with the scope and level of the position. Requirements: Education and Experience: Bachelor's Degree in related field is required. Minimum one-year experience in admissions or services preferred along with a Master's degree. Skills/Abilities: Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Requires organizational skills and good judgment. Ability to be confidential. Ability to work evenings, weekends as well travel out of town when necessary. Valid driver's license required at time of employment. Supervisory Responsibility: May supervise work-study students, interns and student ambassadors. Driving Responsibility: This position requires travel. Must possess a valid driver's license and clean driving record (as defined by University insurance carrier guidelines) Travel: This position requires extensive travel throughout the year. Travel may need to occur during inclement weather. Additional Information: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position EEO Statement Utica University is committed to equal opportunity and creating a welcoming work environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to veteran status, disability, citizenship status, domestic violence victim status, or protected status under applicable local, state, or federal law. Commitment to Supporting and Hiring Veterans Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 to offer options for higher education study to veterans returning from the Second World War. More than seventy years since veterans returned from WWII, this tradition of serving veterans is still held in high regard here at Utica University, and we are proud to welcome veterans as students and as valued members of our faculty and professional staff. Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must upload and include the following information: Submit a resume and cover letter at time of application. Three (3) references are required to be listed on the application. These should be professional references, two of which must be current or former supervisors. Finalist will be contacted prior to reference checking. Offers are contingent on the completion of a post-offer background check, and official transcripts are required upon hire. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Utica University 1600 Burrstone Road, Utica, NY 13502"
