      "title": "Lab and Simulation Coordinator, Pre-Licensure Nursing Programs",
      "description": "Utica University\nJob Posting: Lab and Simulation Coordinator, Pre-Licensure Nursing Programs Utica University \n\tJob Posting: Lab and Simulation Coordinator, Pre-Licensure Nursing Programs Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Lab and Simulation Coordinator, Pre-Licensure Nursing Programs Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Health Professions & Education Locations: Utica, NY Posted: May 5, 2026 Closes: Mar 31, 2028 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Exempt Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $75,000.00 - $75,000.00 Position ID: 200180 Share About Utica University: Located in the heart of Central New York, Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 as Utica College. We offer many of the advantages of a large university, such as undergraduate and graduate degree options, excellent academic programs, and outstanding faculty, but with an intimacy and a high degree of personal attention more closely associated with smaller private institutions. We empower learners to achieve their career and life goals through personally enriching experiences and outstanding educational pathways. At Utica University, we are committed to creating a working and learning environment where all people feel supported. Following our institutional values, we work to support diverse perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences in an equitable, respectful, and inclusive environment, while promoting freedom of expression and encouraging civil discourse. Job Description: Position Summary: The Lab and Simulation Coordinator provides leadership, administration, and oversight of all nursing skills laboratory and simulation learning activities across all pre-licensure nursing programs. This role is responsible for ensuring high-quality, standardized, and evidence-based laboratory and simulation experiences that support student learning, clinical competence, patient safety, and program outcomes. The Coordinator collaborates closely with nursing faculty, program directors, and leadership to integrate lab and simulation experiences across the curriculum and align them with national standards, accreditation requirements, and the AACN Essentials (2021). Didactic teaching responsibilities are included in this role. Responsibilities: Provide leadership and oversight for all nursing skills, laboratory, and simulation activities across pre-licensure programs, ensuring high-quality, consistent, and evidence-based learning experiences. Collaborate with program directors, nursing faculty, and the Director of Academic Operations as needed to design, implement, and evaluate lab and simulation activities, including evidence-based simulation scenarios and skills practice aligned with AACN Essentials (2021), ANA Code of Ethics, and program outcomes. Attend planning meetings with nursing faculty and coordinate with the Director of Academic Operations regarding scheduling and use of campus lab facilities to ensure lab and simulation sessions are integrated smoothly with campus operations. Maintain the master schedule for lab and simulation use, including open lab hours, course labs, simulation sessions, and cross-program utilization, in coordination with the Director of Academic Operations to prevent conflicts with campus events or resource allocation. Ensure lab and simulation environments are adequately prepared, safe, and equipped with functioning technology, equipment, and consumables, and work with the Director of Academic Operations to address any campus-level facility or safety concerns. Maintain inventory and ordering of lab supplies and equipment; develop and manage replacement and maintenance plans for simulation hardware and software, keeping the Director of Academic Operations informed of major needs impacting campus resources. Provide support to lab instructors and student lab assistants, including orientation, training in simulation pedagogy and lab content delivery, performance feedback, and scheduling, while coordinating with the Director of Academic Operations on staffing assignments for campus lab operations. ·Provide faculty development support in lab and simulation instruction, ensuring consistency across instructors and cohorts while aligning with program and accreditation standards. Teach 2-3 (6-9 annually) sections per semester, as assigned, within pre-licensure programs. Collect and review assessment data related to lab and simulation learning, including student competencies, skills check-offs, and simulation outcomes; provide recommendations to program directors and collaborate with the Director of Academic Operations if campus-wide implications arise. Serve as a resource for simulation and lab instructional technology, including troubleshooting, updates, and training faculty on best practices. Collaborate with program directors and the Director of Academic Operations to support quality improvement, accreditation compliance, and consistency across campus operations, without assuming the Director of Academic Operations' responsibility for student conduct, campus facilities, or clinical placements. Perform other duties related specifically to lab and simulation coordination, as required by program directors, coordinating with the Director of Academic Operations when campus-level support or resources are involved. Requirements: Education and Experience: Master's degree in nursing with a current and unencumbered NYS RN license, required. At least 2 years of acute care hospital experience required. BLS credentialed, ACLS preferred. Prior management experience preferred. Teaching experience preferred. Skills/Abilities: Strong computer and technology skills required. Strong organizational skills required. Excellent interpersonal communication skills Experience with Simulation Supervisory Responsibility: Student lab assistants and lab adjuncts Additional Information: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position EEO Statement Utica University is committed to equal opportunity, and creating a welcoming work environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to veteran status, disability, citizenship status, domestic violence victim status, or protected status under applicable local, state, or federal law. Commitment to Supporting and Hiring Veterans Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 to offer options for higher education study to veterans returning from the Second World War. More than seventy years since veterans returned from WWII, this tradition of serving veterans is still held in high regard here at Utica University, and we are proud to welcome veterans as students and as valued members of our faculty and professional staff. Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must upload the following documents: Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Utica University 1600 Burrstone Road, Utica, NY 13502"
    },
    "https://utica.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205828": {
      "title": "Part-Time Circulation Assistant",
      "description": "Utica University\nJob Posting: Part-Time Circulation Assistant Utica University \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time Circulation Assistant Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time Circulation Assistant Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Library Locations: Utica, NY Posted: Oct 15, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Non-Exempt Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $16.00 - $16.00 Position ID: 205828 Share About Utica University: Located in the heart of Central New York, Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 as Utica College. We offer many of the advantages of a large university, such as undergraduate and graduate degree options, excellent academic programs, and outstanding faculty, but with an intimacy and a high degree of personal attention more closely associated with smaller private institutions. We empower learners to achieve their career and life goals through personally enriching experiences and outstanding educational pathways. At Utica University, we are committed to creating a working and learning environment where all people feel supported. Following our institutional values, we work to support diverse perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences in an equitable, respectful, and inclusive environment, while promoting freedom of expression and encouraging civil discourse. Job Description: Position Summary: In this dynamic role, the incumbent will play a vital part in ensuring the smooth operation of our library by assisting students, faculty, and staff with their Access Services and Library needs. Will be responsible for checking out and returning library materials, maintaining accurate records, and providing excellent customer service. Supervises student and graduate assistants during shifts, coordinating with the primary student supervisors. May assist in processing reserves and interlibrary loans.  In charge of the library when a librarian is not on duty. Responsible for opening and closing the library. May cross-train in other areas while still performing the duties of circulation assistant. Monitors and responds to emails in several accounts. Works closely with the Reference Librarian: Coordinator of Access Services and the entire Access Services team to ensure excellent public service, achieve department goals, and advance the library as a space for studying and learning. Responsibilities: Charges and discharges library materials for patrons, including books from the main collection, course reserves, and library laptops. Provides directional information and refers library users to appropriate reference areas. Provides primary point of contact for phone calls to the main library line. Monitors library email accounts. Assists patrons in finding books or journals and provides basic reference assistance when no librarian is on duty. Interprets and enforces library policy when a librarian is not on duty, and is responsible for maintaining an atmosphere conducive to studying and research. Supervises student assistants working in their duties. Assists in shelving, shelf-reading, shifting, and cleaning of collections. Conducts searches for missing materials, identifies materials in need of replacement or repair and forwards to the Coordinator of Circulation Services. Assists with interlibrary loan and reserve processing as needed. Contributes to evaluation of departmental policies and procedures, and creates documentation and records as required. Follows procedures for opening and closing the library at established hours.  Makes sure the building is secure at closing. Reports maintenance issues and relays pertinent information to library staff. Maintains patron records and their confidentiality. Performs other duties as assigned and/or assists with special projects as are required by circumstance. Works with supervisor to develop specific goals that support Utica University's operational plans. This is done at least annually through the annual performance evaluation process, however review of goals will occur throughout the year. Responsible for working with supervisor and other team members to achieve successful results on all established individual and departmental goals and key performance indicators. Requirements: Education and Experience: 2 yr. degree required. Supervisory experience desirable. Skills/Abilities: Adaptability with new and emerging technologies; must be able to work with desktop applications and the internet and demonstrate the ability to learn new systems timely and efficiently. Ability to deal courteously and effectively with a wide variety of constituents. Excellent communication skills. Ability to work accurately with attention to detail. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to adapt to changes in workflow and procedures. Ability to work well independently and in a team environment. Ability to organize time and work assignments effectively. Ability to train and supervise work-study students. Knowledge of library principles, practices, and terminology is desirable. Supervisory Responsibility: Supervises the work of library student assistants. Additional Information: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position EEO Statement Utica University is committed to equal opportunity and creating a welcoming work environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to veteran status, disability, citizenship status, domestic violence victim status, or protected status under applicable local, state, or federal law. Commitment to Supporting and Hiring Veterans Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 to offer options for higher education study to veterans returning from the Second World War. More than seventy years since veterans returned from WWII, this tradition of serving veterans is still held in high regard here at Utica University, and we are proud to welcome veterans as students and as valued members of our faculty and professional staff. Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must upload and include the following information: Submit a resume and cover letter at time of application. Three (3) references are required to be listed on the application. These should be professional references, two of which must be current or former supervisors. Finalist will be contacted prior to reference checking. Offers are contingent on the completion of a post-offer background check, and official transcripts are required upon hire. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Utica University 1600 Burrstone Road, Utica, NY 13502"
