igned based on academic school within the University and will be integrated into the school/major areas of responsibility by attending school-sponsored events and through various interactions and partnerships with faculty. Responsibilities: Completes ongoing assessments of all students in areas of academic/transition needs. Assists students with course registration and academic planning in conjunction with the faculty academic advisor. Assists students with academic coaching and preparedness in areas such as time management, organization, study skills, etc. as needed Follow up and assist students who receive academic alerts in a personal and timely manner. Updates student case notes and takes detailed notes on all student meetings. Attends weekly meetings with the Center for Student Success and School or department meetings as necessary. Triages the needs and questions of all students and helps to direct and connect students with appropriate offices and support programs. Assists with programming, presentations, and events. Takes an active role in the development of the department's strategic and operational plans as required by department leadership. Actively participate in the department's/division's ongoing assessment processes, as required by the unit's supervisor or assessment coordinator. May serves as an instructor for UCC 101- First Year Seminar. Requirements: Education and Experience: Bachelor's degree is required. Master's preferred. Prior experience working with University students in a residential setting and University programming experience is preferred. Skills/Abilities: Excellent interpersonal and communication skills required. Knowledge of Microsoft products such as Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Google Docs, Google Sheets, and Google Drive. Must be knowledgeable and up to date on student retention and persistence trends and strategies in higher education. Preferred knowledge of EAB Navigate, Banner, and Argos. High Consideration to those who have teaching experience or prior experience in student success. Must be able to attend special events outside of normal office hours. This includes weekends and evenings as needed. Supervisory Responsibility: This position does not supervise other full time staff. Additional Information: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position EEO Statement Utica University is committed to equal opportunity and creating a welcoming work environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to veteran status, disability, citizenship status, domestic violence victim status, or protected status under applicable local, state, or federal law. Commitment to Supporting and Hiring Veterans Utica University is a comprehensive, independent, private institution founded in 1946 to offer options for higher education study to veterans returning from the Second World War. More than seventy years since veterans returned from WWII, this tradition of serving veterans is still held in high regard here at Utica University, and we are proud to welcome veterans as students and as valued members of our faculty and professional staff. Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must upload and include the following information: Submit a resume and cover letter at time of application. Three (3) references are required to be listed on the application. These should be professional references, two of which must be current or former supervisors. Finalist will be contacted prior to reference checking. Offers are contingent on the completion of a post-offer background check, and official transcripts are required upon hire. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Utica University 1600 Burrstone Road, Utica, NY 13502"
